{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>And one who comes into the house.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: a house under quarantine (מוסגר) does not impart impurity to one who enters it, as it is stated, ״והבא אל הבית״ — 'and one who comes into the house' — meaning one whose face is directed toward the house. But once it says ״והבא אליו״ — 'and one who comes into it' — after the closing up (פתיחה), if he lingered in it the duration of eating half a loaf (חצי פרס), he is impure — he and his garments and everything upon him, for they too are included in ״והבא אל הבית״; and if he did not linger this duration, he is not impure but he alone."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:24.331748916Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}